package seal.embed;

// A fault a script didn't catch, an exception or an error, as SealScript.run and create throw it:
// its message is what `seal run` prints for it, with the lines it happened at (docs/EMBED.md §12).
// On the JVM it is the compiler's io.github.thelinuxseal.seal.embed.SealException, Java's
// RuntimeException.
class SealException {
    /** Whether the script was stopped: it ran past its limit, or SealScript.stop stopped it. */
    public bit stopped();

    /** What happened, and where. */
    public string getMessage();
}
